@host = http://localhost:5100

### What the register holds
GET {{host}}/installations

### A notification to everyone
POST {{host}}/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "alert",
  "title": "Resultat klara",
  "body": "Ett meddelande fran sample-servern",
  "route": "log",
  "highPriority": true
}

### A notification five seconds from now, so the app can be put in the background first
POST {{host}}/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "alert",
  "title": "Nu syns jag",
  "body": "Appen hann i bakgrunden",
  "route": "log",
  "highPriority": true,
  "delaySeconds": 5
}

### A notification to one tag expression
POST {{host}}/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "alert",
  "targetKind": "tags",
  "target": "kind:news && !team:blue",
  "title": "Bara till nyhetsprenumeranter",
  "body": "team:blue ar undantagna"
}

### A silent message; nothing is shown, the handler runs
POST {{host}}/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "silent",
  "data": { "sync": "everything" }
}

### Rebuild the widgets
POST {{host}}/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "widget",
  "widgetKind": "sample"
}

### Update the Live Activity
POST {{host}}/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "liveactivity",
  "activityKind": "sample",
  "title": "Uppdaterad fran servern",
  "body": "Innehallet kommer utifran"
}

### AI: the exposed Assistant feature (demo provider), one answer
POST {{host}}/ai/features/Assistant
Content-Type: application/json
Spine-Installation: sample-phone

{
  "messages": [
    { "role": "system", "contents": [{ "$type": "text", "text": "Dropped: the server owns the prompt." }] },
    { "role": "user", "contents": [{ "$type": "text", "text": "Vad kan du göra?" }] }
  ]
}

### AI: the same, streamed as server-sent events
POST {{host}}/ai/features/Assistant
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: text/event-stream
Spine-Installation: sample-phone

{
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "contents": [{ "$type": "text", "text": "Vad kan du göra?" }] }
  ]
}

### AI: a feature the server owns. Summary is the demo; Story (Anthropic) and Quick (OpenAI) need keys
POST {{host}}/sample/summary
Content-Type: application/json
Spine-Installation: sample-phone

{
  "facts": ["Startade 10:02", "Missade kontroll 4 med två minuter", "Femma i klassen"],
  "feature": "Summary"
}

### AI: one picture from the Picture feature (OpenAI)
POST {{host}}/sample/picture
Content-Type: application/json

{ "prompt": "En orienteringskontroll i en granskog, akvarell" }

### AI: a token for a realtime voice session (Voice, OpenAI). The app opens "url" with "Authorization: Bearer {token}"
POST {{host}}/ai/realtime/Voice
Spine-Installation: sample-phone

### AI: text read aloud (Read, the demo voice): base64 PCM16 at 24 kHz and a viseme per letter. ReadAzure, once its key is set, has Azure's voice and visemes
POST {{host}}/ai/speech/Read
Content-Type: application/json
Spine-Installation: sample-phone

{ "text": "Hej, jag heter Nova." }

### AI: what was spent, by day, feature and model (localhost only)
GET {{host}}/ai/usage

### Sign-in: sign up with email and password. The code is in the server's log ("Sign-in email (VerifyEmail)")
POST {{host}}/auth/password/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "anna@example.com", "password": "correct horse", "displayName": "Anna" }

### Sign-in: the code from the log; the answer has accessToken and refreshToken
POST {{host}}/auth/password/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "anna@example.com", "code": "PASTE-CODE" }

### Sign-in: email and password
POST {{host}}/auth/password/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "anna@example.com", "password": "correct horse" }

### Sign-in: who the access token says you are
GET {{host}}/sample/me
Authorization: Bearer PASTE-ACCESS-TOKEN

### Sign-in: a new pair for the refresh token (each refresh token works once)
POST {{host}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "PASTE-REFRESH-TOKEN" }

### Sign-in through the browser (Auth:Google:* or Auth:Apple:* in user secrets): open this URL in a browser.
### The provider returns here and the server redirects to 127.0.0.1:53124 with ?code=…; nothing listens there, so copy the code from the address bar.
GET {{host}}/auth/google/start?redirect_uri=http://127.0.0.1:53124/&code_challenge=E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM&code_challenge_method=S256&state=s1

### Sign-in: the browser's code with the verifier behind the challenge above
POST {{host}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "PASTE-CODE", "codeVerifier": "dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27uhbUJU1p1r_wW1gFWFOEjXk", "redirectUri": "http://127.0.0.1:53124/" }

### Sign-in: delete the account
DELETE {{host}}/auth/account
Authorization: Bearer PASTE-ACCESS-TOKEN
